# Cache policy, read by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages at deploy time.
# GitHub Pages ignores this file entirely - see the Caching section in
# README.md for what to do there instead.
#
# "max-age=0, must-revalidate" does NOT mean "don't cache". The browser still
# stores every file; it just asks whether its copy is still good before using
# it, and an unchanged file comes back as a 304 with no body at all. For a
# site this size that costs a few hundred bytes per visit and makes it
# impossible for a returning visitor to run last week's JavaScript against
# this week's index.html - which is the failure that actually bites, because
# the files load as one interdependent set sharing a single global scope.
#
# The fonts could reasonably be cached far longer, since a face is only ever
# replaced by editing fonts.css to point at a new filename. That's left off
# deliberately: it trades a guarantee for ~190KB of transfer, and this file
# is here to buy the guarantee.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
